          "date": "2026-09-03 06:50:44.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-17000 libcfs: carry the dump pid as a pid_t",
        "message": "LU-17000 libcfs: carry the dump pid as a pid_t\n\nlibcfs_debug_dumplog_internal() takes a pid through a void * and prints\nit with %ld, so smatch reports the argument as cast from a pointer.\nTake a pid_t instead, so the value is not laundered through a pointer,\nand use uintptr_t on both sides of the round trip through\nkthread_run().  The dump file name is unchanged.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ia711249186d4b9989f2ac534653ea1744e9983fe\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68508\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
